From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:01:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] DVDDemuxFFmpeg: do not wrap DVD pts that jump back

ffmpeg takes a pts more than a minute below the first one it read as a
wrap of the 33-bit clock and adds 2^33 ticks. DVD pts jump back at title
and cell changes, so after a demuxer opened mid-title a jump back put the
packets 26.5 hours ahead of the VOBU times libdvdnav reports.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,10 @@
   if (iformat && strcmp(iformat->name, "mpegts") == 0)
     av_opt_set_int(m_pFormatContext, "probesize", 10000000, 0); // double ffmpeg default
 
+  // DVD pts jump back at title and cell changes, which ffmpeg would take for a 33-bit wrap
+  if (pInput->IsStreamType(DVDSTREAM_TYPE_DVD))
+    av_opt_set_int(m_pFormatContext, "correct_ts_overflow", 0, 0);
+
   // this should never happen. Log it to inform about the error.
   if (m_pFormatContext->nb_streams > 0 && m_pFormatContext->streams == nullptr)
   {
